sequeler
------------------------------------------
Sequeler is a native Linux SQL client built in Vala and Gtk. It allows you to
connect to your local and remote databases, write SQL in a handy text editor
with language recognition, and visualize SELECT results in a Gtk.Grid Widget.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libcairo2-1.18.6-1
  libgda5.0_4-5.2.10-1
  libgee0.8_2-0.20.1-1
  libglib2.0_0-2.90.1-1
  libgranite6-6.2.0-1bl2
  libgtk3_0-3.24.52-1
  libgtksourceview4.0-4.8.4-1
  libintl8-0.22.5-1
  libsecret1_0-0.18.5-1
  libssh2_1-1.11.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gettext-devel-0.22.5-1
  libcairo-devel-1.18.6-1
  libgda5.0-devel-5.2.10-1
  libgee0.8-devel-0.20.1-1
  libglib2.0-devel-2.90.1-1
  libgranite-devel-6.2.0-1bl2
  libgtk3-devel-3.24.52-1
  libgtksourceview4.0-devel-4.8.4-1
  libsecret1-devel-0.18.5-1
  libssh2-devel-1.11.0-1
  meson-1.10.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  vala-0.56.18-1
  vala-granite-6.2.0-1bl2
  vala-gtksourceview4.0-4.8.4-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/ellie-commons/sequeler

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/ellie-commons/sequeler/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack sequeler-0.9.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./sequeler-0.9.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/sequeler-0.9.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/sequeler-0.9.0-X.tar.xz

